Article 7
(1) The obligations and responsibilities of the Regional Government as referred to in Article 6 letter a, include:
a. establishing policies, programs, and activities for the protection and recovery of women and children from acts of violence;
b. implementing policies for the protection and recovery of women and children from acts of violence established by the government; c. conducting cooperation in the implementation of protection and recovery of women and children from acts of violence;
d. providing support for facilities and infrastructure for the implementation of protection and recovery of women and children from acts of violence;
e. allocating budget for the implementation of protection of women and children from acts of violence in accordance with the financial capacity of the Region; and
f. fostering, supervising, evaluating the implementation of protection and recovery of women and children from acts of violence. (2) In order to carry out the obligations and responsibilities as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regent shall establish a Regional action plan as the basis for SKPD and UKPD.
(3) The Regional action plan as referred to in paragraph (2) shall be prepared by involving non-governmental organizations as well as parties who are concerned and carry out assistance work for women and children, with a term of duty of 3 (three) years.
(4) Implementation and technical instructions for the Regional action plan as referred to in paragraph (2) shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

CHAPTER XI
GUIDANCE AND SUPERVISION
Article 19
(1) Regional Government is obligated to conduct guidance and supervision of the implementation of protection of women and children from violence.
(2) Guidance as referred to in paragraph (1), includes:
a. guidelines and fulfillment standards;
b. technical guidance;
c. education and training;
d. provision of facilities;
e. monitoring; and
f. evaluation.
(3) In order to realize the objectives of protection of women and children from acts of violence, guidance as referred to in paragraph (2) shall be implemented in accordance with minimum service standards.

